      83.16,
      598.1,
      518.32,
      613.57
    ],
    "text": "absolute entered against a defendant for non-appearance cannot be challenged on merits,",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.600000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      83.3,
      618.73,
      521.66,
      634.21
    ],
    "text": "but could have been set aside by curing the default by taking steps under section 389 of",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.600000381469727,
      12.18452262878418
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      83.25,
      639.63,
      445.57,
      655.1
    ],
    "text": "the Civil Procedure Code by summary procedure within a reasonable time.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.600000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      83.89,
      680.19,
      519.76,
      695.66
    ],
    "text": "The learned counsel for the respondent submitted that when the respondent learnt about",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.600000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      83.93,
      699.39,
      519.96,
      714.86
    ],
    "text": "the decree absolute the appealable period had lapsed. Hence the petitioner was compelled",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.600000381469727
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      511.75,
      739.94,
      520.45,
      755.42
    ],
    "text": "3",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.600000381469727
    ]
